{"parentUuid":"4e942105-bc96-484e-8ba7-9ed543311a96","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Yjb4z61WNiD8TLthhp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019zJgWLLNJ3nmfzmn8C9goR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A .github/workflows/pages.yml CLAUDE.md stops subsystems tools && git status --short | grep -v \"^[AM] \" ; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nAdd the museum photo overlay to every stop; bump workflow actions\n\nEvery stop now has a CC-licensed museum photo (Wikimedia Commons, credited on the\npage) with a fitted camera, so the mechanism can be seen on the real car.\n\n- Photo fits for the 14 new photos; the fit tool gains an optional focalPrior.\n- Ghost outlines traced from the photos (220 S gains one; 300 SL, 300 SLR, 260 D,\n  C 111 split into body and cabin; van, Victoria, Blitzen-Benz, SSK, Benz 1886 redrawn).\n- Subsystems handle onPhoto: differential, steering, air suspension and crash fade\n  their wheels; air suspension and the crash car keep the body still; aero hides\n  its road markings.\n- Engine: flywheelR sizes the enclosed Daimler case; flywheels are see-through.\n- SSK wheelbase corrected to 2,950 mm (Mercedes-Benz archive); van radiator moved\n  to the front as photographed.\n- Workflow: upload-artifact v7, configure-pages v6, upload-pages-artifact v5,\n  deploy-pages v5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit the photo overlay work and push to main","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_read_input_tokens":362492,"output_tokens":653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_inp